    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299">

                <pb facs="0657" n="625" xml:id="pg625"/>

                <head>299. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Pakistan<anchor n="1" xml:id="d299-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-03-11T18:27:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 11,
                                1958—6:27 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2293. At Ankara Noon raised with
                    Secretary possibility USG buying Pakistan’s
                    exportable surplus cotton which he estimated 700,000 tons.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d299-f2"/> You may inform Noon: <list>
                        <label>(a)</label>
                        <item>Department has carefully looked into matter as Secretary
                            promised;</item>
                        <label>(b)</label>
                        <item>Information available to Department and Embassy, subject GOP correction, indicates no burdensome
                            surplus Pak cotton at present time;</item>
                        <label>(c)</label>
                        <item>Because its own cotton problems, USG
                            regrets it not in position buy exportable surplus cotton from any
                            country;</item>
                        <label>(d)</label>
                        <item>In informal manner and as appropriate Department and Embassy officials
                            will continue try to provide helpful advice to permit GOP retain and strengthen various aspects
                            its trade ties with free world.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d299-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d299-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 890D.2321/3–1158. Secret. Drafted by
                        Henry W. Spielman and approved by
                        Rountree.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d299-f2" n="2" xml:id="d299-f2-content">
                <p>The meeting took place on January 28. (Department of State, Secretary’s Memoranda
                    of Conversation: Lot 64 D 199)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
